From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 11:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 141/142] soc: mediatek: tolerate a no-source BTIF interrupt
 during a WMT exchange

The first Phase B boot stopped WMT common init at step 5 with -EPROTO
after 16 of the command's 26 bytes had been written. The second service,
entered from the BTIF interrupt, read an IIR with no RX, timeout or
THR-empty source pending, and the strict guard retired the exchange
before any byte was received. An interrupt raised before the previous
service drained its cause reports "no interrupt pending" by the time the
handler reads IIR again.

Treat only that case as benign on a non-initial service: IIR bit 0 set
with bits 1, 2 and 6 clear. Count it, consume the same service and
deadline budget, touch no FIFO or register, make no protocol transition
and retransmit nothing; the next pending source continues the exchange.
Every other unexpected cause still retires with -EPROTO.

Record the last IIR and the no-source count in the exchange state and
print them in the existing common-init failure footer, so the next
failure shows the cause without new register reads.

Unsigned experiment draft; archive identity is non-certifying.
---
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-consys.c      |  6 ++++--
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-wmt-full-io.h | 10 ++++++++++
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-consys.c b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-consys.c
index bbba770b4..8b607f8dc 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-consys.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-consys.c
@@ -1509,9 +1509,11 @@ static int mt6797_consys_common_init(struct device *dev, struct mt6797_consys *o
 	print_hex_dump(KERN_INFO, "WMT common init calibration RX: ", DUMP_PREFIX_OFFSET,
 		       16, 1, ci->calibration, ci->calibration_bytes, false);
 	if (ret && ci->completed < WMT_INIT_STEPS && ci->io.prepared) {
-		dev_info(dev, "WMT common init failed step %u: tx=%u rx=%u services=%u frames=%u\n",
+		dev_info(dev,
+			 "WMT common init failed step %u: tx=%u rx=%u services=%u frames=%u iir=0x%08x no-source=%u\n",
 			 ci->completed, ci->io.tx_count, ci->io.rx_count,
-			 ci->io.services, ci->io.frames);
+			 ci->io.services, ci->io.frames, ci->io.last_iir,
+			 ci->io.no_source_services);
 		print_hex_dump(KERN_INFO, "WMT common init failed RX: ", DUMP_PREFIX_OFFSET,
 			       16, 1, ci->io.received, ci->io.rx_count, false);
 	}
diff --git a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-wmt-full-io.h b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-wmt-full-io.h
index 3f17b75e0..d894dafc3 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-wmt-full-io.h
+++ b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-wmt-full-io.h
@@ -36,6 +36,7 @@ struct mt6797_wmt_full_io {
 	const unsigned char *expected;
 	unsigned int task, prefix;
 	unsigned int expected_length, rx_count, consumed, frames, services, tx_count;
+	unsigned int last_iir, no_source_services;
 	unsigned long deadline;
 	/* Serializes FIFO progress, terminal state and process timeout. */
 	spinlock_t lock;
@@ -202,6 +203,15 @@ static void mt6797_wmt_full_service(struct mt6797_wmt_full_io *io, int initial)
 	}
 	io->services++;
 	iir = readl(io->btif + 8);
+	io->last_iir = iir;
+	/* An already-delivered IRQ can outlive its FIFO source. It conveys no
+	 * bytes or protocol event. Keep the same service/deadline budget and
+	 * wait for a pending source; never retransmit or fabricate progress.
+	 */
+	if (!initial && (iir & 0x47) == 1) {
+		io->no_source_services++;
+		return;
+	}
 	if ((initial && (iir & 0x44)) || (!initial && !(iir & 0x46))) {
 		mt6797_wmt_full_retire(io, -EPROTO);
 		return;
